## Issues

### Bloat findings (this brevity sweep)

- [ ] `description` is ~1,182 chars (cap 200) — a single paragraph enumerating
  every artifact the CLI installs (pointer stub, methodology doc set, slash
  commands, agents, skills, MCP entry, tree launcher, IDE wiring), every
  thing it never does (write `.mcp.json` brain entry, scaffold entry-point
  artifacts, create brain root, ask backend-specific values), every flag it
  doesn't accept, the warning shape, and per-category follow-up surfaces.
  This is a comprehensive feature spec, not a description.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (CLI flag enumerations, file paths, MCP key strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `intent` is ~828 words across multiple paragraphs (cap 100, single
  paragraph). Restates the description verbatim with added paragraphs about
  storage-agnostic vocabulary, `.aide/config/` ownership, terminal warning
  shape, idempotency, and what the user does next. Trim to a single ten-second
  north-star paragraph naming what the cold-start CLI is *for* — the no-agent
  install surface — and let outcomes carry the rest.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 16 items (cap 4). Each is paragraph length and
  enumerates exact subdirectory paths (`.claude/commands/aide/`,
  `.claude/agents/aide/`, `.aide/docs/`, `.aide/bin/aide-tree.mjs`,
  `.aide/config/brain.aide`), exact MCP keys (`aide`, `aidemd-mcp`), exact
  flag spellings (`--ide`, `--brain`, `--brain-path`, `--vault-path`,
  `--brain-root`, `--brain-token`, `--brain-url`, `--brain-name`), exact
  install-service step names (`aide_init({ category: "brain" })`, "the
  brain.aide-scaffold InitStep", "the MCP-entry-plan InitStep"), exact
  YAML null index numbers (`args[3]`), and exact warning prose categories.
  Compress to 3-4 falsifiable domain criteria.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (file paths, CLI flags, function names, MCP key strings, exact strings, argument indexes)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 12 items, all paragraph length, almost all citing
  retired prior-design names or specific regression classes (`<BRAIN_PATH>`,
  `<API_TOKEN>`, `<VAULT_ROOT>`, `${BRAIN_PATH}`, `__UNWIRED__`, magic UUIDs,
  retired step builders by name, exact arg-index forbidden, exact flag-name
  enumerations, exact MCP key dual-check). Forbidden content per the contract.
  Trim to 3-4 falsifiable failure modes; let plan and code own the
  retired-symbol-rejection logic.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (retired prior designs, migration history, exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Context` is ~600+ words (cap ~150). Recapitulates the cold-start gap,
  the agent-bandwidth contrast, the methodology layer enumeration, the
  brain-layer-as-deferred argument, and the YAML-null-as-structural-signal
  story. All of this duplicates content already in `src/.aide` and the
  (rewritten) project root.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat, spec-gap
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `## Strategy` has ~10 paragraph-length decisions (cap ~5 ≤80 words each).
  Each decision is multiple thousand words and encodes implementation
  contracts: which `InitStep` to apply, which to skip, which flag values to
  accept, MCP merge logic, file-presence-check shape, JSON parse-error abort
  contract, terminal warning rendering details. These are plan-level.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce full terminal output
  blocks with exact prose, exact warning ASCII borders, exact category labels,
  exact follow-up surface names. Per the contract, examples should be 2-3
  brief pattern illustrations, not byte-faithful UI mockups.
  Traces to: `## Good examples`, `## Bad examples` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with `src/.aide` and the (rewritten) project root:
  the YAML-null-as-unwired-slot signal, the `--brain <integration>` no-backend-value
  rule, the `.aide/config/` ownership boundary, the four-state brain status
  vocabulary, the visible-command-boundary invariant for sync, the
  `mcpServers["brain"]` no-write rule — all are restated verbatim from
  parents. Push to parents; this leaf should commit only to what's specific
  to the cold-start surface.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy, Bad examples | Sibling-redundancy doctrine
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

### Carry-forward (real implementation issues, still open)

- [ ] `src/cli/init/index.ts:258-259 (warningSkipped filter)` — `exists`
  (byte-identical) results are excluded from the warning's Skipped files
  section. The spec's good example shows `[exists]` files explicitly listed
  in the warning, but the current filter routes only `skipped-drift` and
  `skipped-missing-canonical` to `warningSkipped`. This is real
  implementation-drift that should land in a future plan; survives the
  brevity rewrite because the underlying contract ("CLI reports skipped
  files in the warning") is a falsifiable domain outcome.
  Traces to: outcomes about per-category warning content
  Misalignment: implementation-drift

- [ ] `src/cli/init/index.ts (no parseIde call)` — `--ide <choice>` is named
  as a recognized flag in outcomes and help text, but no `parseIde()` exists
  and the IIFE never reads `--ide`. IDE is permanently deferred regardless
  of flag, so `Already set up.` is structurally unreachable. Real plan-gap
  (no plan implements `--ide`); survives brevity rewrite if outcomes preserve
  the "supplying `--ide` resolves the IDE deferral" contract.
  Traces to: outcomes about flag handling and idempotency
  Misalignment: plan-gap

## Retro

This spec is the most extreme bloat in the tree because it tried to be a
single-document recipe for the cold-start CLI — every flag, every artifact,
every warning category, every retired regression class, every step builder.
The result is a 71KB spec for a CLI that orchestrates a dozen file writes.

The strategist treated negative-example density as a quality signal — the more
bad shapes the spec rules out by name, the safer the outcome. The Brevity
Contract's outcomes-purpose test is the right defense: most of those
negative examples (literal sentinel names, retired step builders, forbidden
arg-index introspection, forbidden flag list) are caught by unit tests and
type checks; they belong in test code with comments, not in spec outcomes.

Recommended sequence: rewrite this leaf AFTER the project root and `src/.aide`
have been pruned, because both parents currently restate brain-layer doctrine
this spec leans on. Once the parents own brain-layer invariants, this leaf
can shrink to "no-agent terminal install of the methodology layer plus the
bundled brain template scaffold; deferred surfaces named in a final warning."
The two carry-forward implementation issues survive the rewrite as
plan/implementation work.
